erall, the product demonstrates positive potential if the identified sensory drivers are addressed.	Product development should prioritize increasing product softness, as 38% of consumers identified it as 'too low' with a moderate penalty of 0.67. Additionally, the flavor intensity requires recalibration, with 25% of respondents finding it lacking (penalty 0.8). Avoid adjustments to the 'high' side of these attributes, as they are not currently driving significant negative impact. Following these adjustments, conduct a follow-up sensory panel with a larger, verified participant pool to mitigate the data quality concerns noted in this phase.	CONTINUE_REFINEMENT	2026-04-21 05:35:28.525	2026-05-18 05:20:29.845
